<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro" name="athena">

  <xacro:arg name="sim" default="false"/>
  <xacro:property name="is_sim" value="$(arg sim)"/>

  <!--
    Athena rover description.

    This file does two jobs and only one of them matters to navigation:

      1. It places the SENSOR FRAMES.  camera_link is where the costmap
         believes every depth point came from, imu_link is where the EKF
         believes the gyro is, gps_link is where navsat_transform believes
         the antenna is.  These are load-bearing.  Measure them, do not
         guess them.

      2. It draws a rover.  The body, wheels and nose block are cosmetic.
         Nothing reads them.  They exist because a recognisable shape makes
         it obvious at a glance which way the rover is facing.

    Frame tree this produces:

        odom  (ekf_local owns this link)
          |
        base_link ...... chassis centre, base_height above the ground
          |- base_footprint  ground projection
          |- camera_link     RealSense D435i    <- drives obstacle avoidance
          |- imu_link        Pixhawk            <- drives the EKF yaw rate
          |- gps_link        GPS antenna        <- drives navsat_transform
          |- nose_marker, wheel_* x6   (visual only)

    Editing rule: XML comments cannot contain a double hyphen anywhere, not
    just at the end.  xacro fails with a "not well-formed (invalid token)"
    error that points at the comment, not at the real problem.  Use a single
    hyphen or a comma.
  -->

  <!-- =====================================================================
       MEASURED NUMBERS.  Everything below is derived from these.
       Each one says how it was established.  If you change the hardware,
       change it here, then rebuild athena_gps_nav from the workspace root
       with a symlink install (see CONTRIBUTING.md) and relaunch.
       ===================================================================== -->

  <!-- Chassis. Tape measured 2026-09-02, and it agrees with both
       athena_drive's saved track_width and nav2_params' footprint. -->
  <xacro:property name="base_length"  value="1.30"/>  <!-- x, front to back -->
  <xacro:property name="base_width"   value="1.00"/>  <!-- y, side to side  -->
  <xacro:property name="base_height"  value="0.25"/>  <!-- ground to base_link with 30cm wheels -->
  <xacro:property name="track_width"  value="0.85"/>  <!-- wheel centre to centre -->

  <!-- Camera: RealSense D435i, front centre.  Both numbers below are owner
       tape measurements, 2026-09-03: the lens is 0.50 m forward of the
       chassis centre (so 0.15 m back from the front face) and 0.65 m above
       the ground, hence camera_z = 0.65 - base_height.

       camera_x was 0.10 until 2026-09-03, i.e. 0.40 m behind where the lens
       actually is.  Every depth point was marked that much closer to the
       rover than it really was, so returns from just past the front bumper
       landed INSIDE the Nav2 footprint and the controller read them as a
       collision it could not drive out of. -->
  <xacro:property name="camera_x"     value="0.50"/>
  <xacro:property name="camera_z"     value="0.55"/>
  <!-- Camera tilt about its own left axis, radians.  ROS sign convention:
       POSITIVE pitch is nose DOWN.  A lot of the confusion in this file's
       history came from getting that backwards.

       0.0 because the camera is currently mounted level, in normal
       landscape (owner, 2026-09-03).

       This was -0.10 until 2026-09-03, i.e. the model believed the camera
       was tilted 5.7 degrees UP when it is in fact level.  That rotates
       every depth point upward by the same angle, and the error grows with
       range: the floor 2 m ahead of the lens lands at z = +0.10 m in
       base_link instead of -0.10 m, which is exactly min_obstacle_height.
       So flat ground from about 2 m out was being marked LETHAL, in a
       band right across the camera's field of view.  Together with the
       camera_x error that band sat about 2 m in front of the bumper, the
       controller refused to drive into it, and Nav2 fell through to its
       Spin recovery, which turns 1.57 rad to the left.

       WHEN YOU TILT THE CAMERA DOWN (planned, to spot low objects like a
       hammer near the wheels): put the REAL angle here as a POSITIVE
       number, and measure it, do not eyeball it.  Guessing brings the
       phantom wall straight back, and a downward tilt makes it worse
       because more of the frame is floor.  Run
       indoor_test/mount_check.py camera after remounting; it reads the
       tilt off the floor plane and prints the value to paste here.
       Note also that min_obstacle_height (0.10 m in nav2_params.yaml) sits
       0.20 m above the ground, so a hammer will still be invisible until
       that is lowered as well.  Lower it only once this angle is measured,
       not before, or you will be marking the floor on purpose. -->
  <xacro:property name="camera_pitch" value="0.0"/>

  <!-- Pixhawk: same place as the camera, 15 cm lower (owner, 2026-09-03).
       Only the ORIENTATION of this frame affects navigation: the EKF rotates
       the gyro into base_link with it, and fuses yaw rate.  The translation
       is cosmetic here because no accelerometer channel is fused, but it is
       written honestly so nobody has to re-derive it later.
       imu_rpy is zero, which asserts the board is bolted down flat with its
       forward arrow pointing at the front of the rover.  If it is rotated or
       inverted, put the real angles here, because a Pixhawk mounted upside
       down reports yaw rate with the wrong sign and the rover will turn away
       from its goal instead of toward it. -->
  <xacro:property name="imu_x"        value="${camera_x}"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_z"        value="${camera_z - 0.15}"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_roll"     value="0.0"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_pitch"    value="0.0"/>
  <xacro:property name="imu_yaw"      value="0.0"/>

  <!-- GPS antenna, relative to base_link.  navsat_transform uses this to
       remove the antenna lever arm from the fix.  NOT YET MEASURED: it is a
       guess that the antenna is over the chassis centre.  Harmless for local
       obstacle avoidance, worth a tape measure before waypoint work. -->
  <xacro:property name="gps_x"        value="0.0"/>
  <xacro:property name="gps_y"        value="0.0"/>
  <xacro:property name="gps_z"        value="0.25"/>

  <!-- Wheel dimensions: 30 cm diameter (radius 0.15 m), 8 cm width -->
  <xacro:property name="base_thick"      value="0.12"/>
  <xacro:property name="wheel_radius"    value="0.15"/>  <!-- 30 cm diameter -->
  <xacro:property name="wheel_width"     value="0.08"/>  <!-- 8 cm width -->
  <xacro:property name="wheel_x"         value="0.45"/>  <!-- front/rear axle offset -->

  <!-- Rocker-Bogie main pivot: 28 cm below depth camera -->
  <xacro:property name="rocker_pivot_x"  value="0.05"/>
  <xacro:property name="rocker_pivot_z"  value="${camera_z - 0.28}"/>

  <material name="athena_body">  <color rgba="0.22 0.25 0.28 1.0"/></material>
  <material name="athena_accent"><color rgba="0.31 0.75 0.80 1.0"/></material>
  <material name="athena_wheel"> <color rgba="0.10 0.10 0.11 1.0"/></material>
  <material name="athena_gps">   <color rgba="0.95 0.72 0.20 1.0"/></material>

  <!-- ==== chassis ======================================================= -->

  <link name="base_link">
    <visual>
      <geometry><box size="${base_length} ${base_width} ${base_thick}"/></geometry>
      <material name="athena_body"/>
    </visual>
    <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
      <collision>
        <geometry><box size="${base_length} ${base_width} ${base_thick}"/></geometry>
      </collision>
      <inertial>
        <mass value="45.0"/>
        <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <inertia ixx="${45.0 * (base_width*base_width + base_thick*base_thick) / 12.0}"
                 ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                 iyy="${45.0 * (base_length*base_length + base_thick*base_thick) / 12.0}"
                 iyz="0.0"
                 izz="${45.0 * (base_length*base_length + base_width*base_width) / 12.0}"/>
      </inertial>
    </xacro:if>
  </link>

  <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
    <gazebo reference="base_link">
      <material>Gazebo/DarkGrey</material>
      <mu1>0.5</mu1>
      <mu2>0.5</mu2>
    </gazebo>
  </xacro:if>

  <!-- base_link is the PARENT of base_footprint, not the child.  ekf_local
       publishes odom to base_link, so making base_footprint a parent would
       give base_link two parents.  TF2 requires exactly one, and the result
       is that base_footprint gets orphaned and every lookup involving it
       throws ConnectivityException.  That bites because Nav2 configs
       commonly use base_footprint as robot_base_frame. -->
  <link name="base_footprint"/>
  <joint name="base_footprint_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child  link="base_footprint"/>
    <origin xyz="0 0 ${-base_height}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- A nose block, so "forward" is unmistakable in a 3D view.  A bare box
       looks the same from both ends and you cannot tell a reversing rover
       from an advancing one. -->
  <link name="nose_marker">
    <visual>
      <geometry><box size="0.06 ${base_width * 0.6} 0.04"/></geometry>
      <material name="athena_accent"/>
    </visual>
    <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
      <collision>
        <geometry><box size="0.06 ${base_width * 0.6} 0.04"/></geometry>
      </collision>
    </xacro:if>
  </link>
  <joint name="nose_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child  link="nose_marker"/>
    <origin xyz="${base_length/2 - 0.02} 0 ${base_thick/2}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ==== rocker-bogie suspension and six wheels ====================== -->

  <material name="athena_rocker"><color rgba="0.18 0.20 0.22 1.0"/></material>

  <xacro:macro name="rocker_bogie_assembly" params="side y_sign">
    <!-- Rocker link and main pivot joint -->
    <link name="rocker_${side}">
      <visual>
        <!-- Beam from pivot forward to front wheel -->
        <origin xyz="0.20 0 -0.185" rpy="0 0.74 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.55 0.04 0.04"/></geometry>
        <material name="athena_rocker"/>
      </visual>
      <visual>
        <!-- Beam from pivot backward to bogie joint -->
        <origin xyz="-0.10 0 -0.11" rpy="0 -0.83 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.30 0.04 0.04"/></geometry>
        <material name="athena_rocker"/>
      </visual>
      <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
        <collision>
          <origin xyz="0.20 0 -0.185" rpy="0 0.74 0"/>
          <geometry><box size="0.55 0.04 0.04"/></geometry>
        </collision>
        <inertial>
          <mass value="3.0"/>
          <origin xyz="0.10 0 -0.10" rpy="0 0 0"/>
          <inertia ixx="0.02" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0" iyy="0.08" iyz="0.0" izz="0.08"/>
        </inertial>
      </xacro:if>
    </link>

    <xacro:unless value="${is_sim}">
      <joint name="rocker_${side}_joint" type="fixed">
        <parent link="base_link"/>
        <child  link="rocker_${side}"/>
        <origin xyz="${rocker_pivot_x} ${y_sign * track_width/2} ${rocker_pivot_z}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:unless>

    <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
      <joint name="rocker_${side}_joint" type="revolute">
        <parent link="base_link"/>
        <child  link="rocker_${side}"/>
        <origin xyz="${rocker_pivot_x} ${y_sign * track_width/2} ${rocker_pivot_z}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <axis xyz="0 1 0"/>
        <limit lower="-0.45" upper="0.45" effort="120.0" velocity="5.0"/>
        <dynamics damping="1.0" friction="0.5"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:if>

    <!-- Bogie link and pivot joint -->
    <link name="bogie_${side}">
      <visual>
        <!-- Beam from bogie pivot forward to mid wheel and rear to back wheel -->
        <origin xyz="-0.075 0 -0.075" rpy="0 0.0 0"/>
        <geometry><box size="0.48 0.04 0.04"/></geometry>
        <material name="athena_rocker"/>
      </visual>
      <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
        <collision>
          <origin xyz="-0.075 0 -0.075" rpy="0 0.0 0"/>
          <geometry><box size="0.48 0.04 0.04"/></geometry>
        </collision>
        <inertial>
          <mass value="2.5"/>
          <origin xyz="-0.075 0 -0.075" rpy="0 0 0"/>
          <inertia ixx="0.015" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0" iyy="0.05" iyz="0.0" izz="0.05"/>
        </inertial>
      </xacro:if>
    </link>

    <xacro:unless value="${is_sim}">
      <joint name="bogie_${side}_joint" type="fixed">
        <parent link="rocker_${side}"/>
        <child  link="bogie_${side}"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.20 0.0 -0.22" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:unless>

    <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
      <joint name="bogie_${side}_joint" type="revolute">
        <parent link="rocker_${side}"/>
        <child  link="bogie_${side}"/>
        <origin xyz="-0.20 0.0 -0.22" rpy="0 0 0"/>
        <axis xyz="0 1 0"/>
        <limit lower="-0.45" upper="0.45" effort="100.0" velocity="5.0"/>
        <dynamics damping="1.0" friction="0.5"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:if>

    <!-- Front Wheel attached to Rocker -->
    <xacro:wheel_instance name="wheel_front_${side}" parent="rocker_${side}"
                          x="0.40" y="0.0" z="-0.37"/>

    <!-- Mid Wheel attached to Bogie -->
    <xacro:wheel_instance name="wheel_mid_${side}" parent="bogie_${side}"
                          x="0.15" y="0.0" z="-0.15"/>

    <!-- Rear Wheel attached to Bogie -->
    <xacro:wheel_instance name="wheel_rear_${side}" parent="bogie_${side}"
                          x="-0.30" y="0.0" z="-0.15"/>
  </xacro:macro>

  <!-- Wheel instance macro (30 cm diameter, 3.5 kg mass) -->
  <xacro:macro name="wheel_instance" params="name parent x y z">
    <link name="${name}">
      <visual>
        <geometry><cylinder radius="${wheel_radius}" length="${wheel_width}"/></geometry>
        <material name="athena_wheel"/>
      </visual>
      <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
        <collision>
          <geometry><cylinder radius="${wheel_radius}" length="${wheel_width}"/></geometry>
        </collision>
        <inertial>
          <mass value="3.5"/>
          <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
          <inertia ixx="0.0215" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                   iyy="0.0215" iyz="0.0"
                   izz="0.0394"/>
        </inertial>
      </xacro:if>
    </link>

    <xacro:unless value="${is_sim}">
      <joint name="${name}_joint" type="fixed">
        <parent link="${parent}"/>
        <child  link="${name}"/>
        <origin xyz="${x} ${y} ${z}" rpy="1.5708 0 0"/>
      </joint>
    </xacro:unless>

    <xacro:if value="${is_sim}">
      <joint name="${name}_joint" type="continuous">
        <parent link="${parent}"/>
        <child  link="${name}"/>
        <origin xyz="${x} ${y} ${z}" rpy="1.5708 0 0"/>
        <axis xyz="0 0 1"/>
        <dynamics damping="0.08" friction="0.05"/>
        <limit effort="50.0" velocity="20.0"/>
      </joint>
      <gazebo reference="${name}">
        <material>Gazebo/Black</material>
        <mu1>1.0</mu1>
        <mu2>0.2</mu2>
        <kp>1000000.0</kp>
        <kd>100.0</kd>
        <minDepth>0.005</minDepth>
      </gazebo>
    </xacro:if>
  </xacro:macro>

  <xacro:rocker_bogie_assembly side="left"  y_sign="1"/>
  <xacro:rocker_bogie_assembly side="right" y_sign="-1"/>

  <!-- ==== sensors ======================================================= -->

  <!-- The RealSense driver hangs its own optical frames under camera_link
       (via the camera_link to camera_camera_link bridge in sensors.launch.py),
       so this joint is the only thing standing between the depth cloud and
       the costmap. -->
  <link name="camera_link">
    <visual>
      <geometry><box size="0.025 0.09 0.025"/></geometry>
      <material name="athena_accent"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="camera_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child  link="camera_link"/>
    <origin xyz="${camera_x} 0 ${camera_z}" rpy="0 ${camera_pitch} 0"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="imu_link"/>
  <joint name="imu_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child  link="imu_link"/>
    <origin xyz="${imu_x} 0 ${imu_z}"
            rpy="${imu_roll} ${imu_pitch} ${imu_yaw}"/>
  </joint>

  <link name="gps_link">
    <visual>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.035" length="0.015"/></geometry>
      <material name="athena_gps"/>
    </visual>
  </link>
  <joint name="gps_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child  link="gps_link"/>
    <origin xyz="${gps_x} ${gps_y} ${gps_z}" rpy="0 0 0"/>
  </joint>

</robot>
